{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404250-how-to-interpret-devil-tigers","id":1404250,"title":"How to interpret Devil-Tigers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-23T09:58:17-07:00","id":1404250,"title":"How to interpret Devil-Tigers?","content":"Devil-Tigers is an anti-hero style Road/Dharma and I love it very much. How will you understand and roleplay it? <br /> <br /> For example, use evil power to fight against evil beings is cool, but the boundary between evil user and true evil worshipper is slim. How to balance it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:19:02-07:00","id":1404254,"title":"","content":"Taken at face value, I imagine the Devil-Tigers viewing the Yomi Kings and other infernal beings as rivals who they hope to overthrow and replace one day.<br /> <br /> In attempt to make them acceptable for play here and now, one could posit a &quot;Path of Night&quot; variant where the Devil-Kings seek to serve the August Personage's vision for the world by being better demons than the demons themselves, guiding the world through the dark side of the Wheel of Ages so that it can turn again toward harmony, but this could just as easily be the outlook of a heretical outsider character who's strayed from the original dharma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:56:06-07:00","id":1404262,"title":"","content":"I really didn't get them until I read how they were viewed by other Dharmas in their perspective books. The thrashing dragon description is pretty spot on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T11:29:14-07:00","id":1404268,"title":"","content":"They view themselves as performing the role the hells were supposed to, heavens punishment on the wicked (at least that's my read)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T19:21:48-07:00","id":1404338,"title":"","content":"They've always reminded me of a line from John LeCarre's The Spy Who Came in From the Cold.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;We do disagreeable things so that ordinary people here and elsewhere can sleep safely in their beds at night. Is that too romantic? Of course, we occasionally do <b>very wicked things</b>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And a line from the tv series Homicide: Life on the Street.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Virtue isn't virtue unless it slams up against vice. So consequently, your virtue's not real virtue unless it's been tested. Tempted.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Devil Tigers exist to test humanity, and to temper the virtuous who pass those tests and to torment the weak and the wicked who fail them. It is a public service performed in accordance with the dictates of Heaven in order to maintain and encourage righteousness. But if you're the one being tested - or worse, tormented - then all you see is a monster. <br /> And this is a bit of a double edged sword. They probably have to constantly test each other to insure that they're being righteous monsters instead of petty and wicked ones. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T20:03:24-07:00","id":1404343,"title":"","content":"Sabbat for the East and better then thesabbat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2782,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey","user":"Pittmonkey","date":". 07-24-2020, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2782-pittmonkey","name":"Pittmonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2782_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T20:38:29-07:00","id":1404349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404250-how-to-interpret-devil-tigers?p=1404338#post1404338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is a bit of a double edged sword. They probably have to constantly test each other to insure that they're being righteous monsters instead of petty and wicked ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember that was the point of the comic in the opening of the Devil Tiger Dharma book, that petty wickedness doesn't get you anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T22:34:16-07:00","id":1404363,"title":"","content":"I understand the Devil Tigers philosophy as close to the Path of the Blood of the Assamites. They are monsters, and judges, and they believe superior and doing something valuable by divine mandate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T19:35:18-07:00","id":1404867,"title":"","content":"KotE is a tricky thing to square with the morality systems in Vampire because the eastern philosophy tends to go several layers deeper than most people want to think about.<br /> <br /> For example let's say there is a boss of a small criminal group in the devil tigers city, what do they do since they are supposed to punish the wicked and the evil?<br /> <br /> 1. Criminal breaks laws and there for is evil and can be killed, tortured, and have their soul ripped out with impunity.<br /> This is the simplest ethical viewing of the Devil Tigers, but in truth misses most of their philosophy.<br /> <br /> 2. The mob boss is a source of crime, but they keep worse groups from moving in, thus they should be protected or at least ignored.<br /> This view shows how perception is key to understanding what is the lesser evil and how some &quot;evils&quot; are needed by a functional society. In many instances in history, criminal groups assisted in winning wars or changing political balances. Alternatively in many ethnic communities criminal gangs start out by doing things like ripping off warehouses to distribute things like food or medicine their community.<br /> <br /> 3. The mob boss has been relatively harmless for a long time, but if they switch to worse things like drugs or human trafficking, then its time to die.<br /> This is the most in line with what the Devil Tigers should be, they watch and wait for the line to be crossed, and once that happens, they can do their work with a smile.<br /> <br /> If you want character examples from out side of WoD, I would suggest Konrad Kurze from Warhammer 40K or Hannibal Lector from the Hannibal tv series. You could even make an argument that Stallones character from Demolition Man is a potential example of the notion that you send a monster to fight another monster, or in the quote from the movie &quot;send a maniac to catch one&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T09:27:38-07:00","id":1405077,"title":"","content":"The way I read it came close to Piers Anthony's 'Incarnations of Immortality' series and the <a href=\"https://incarnations.fandom.com/wiki/Incarnation_of_Evil\" target=\"_blank\">incarnation of evil</a>. Something of a necessary 'evil' (pardon the pun) for the functioning of the world but not necessarily something that the entity might truly believe or enjoy. Some might love embracing the Devil Tiger path. Some may see it simply as a job and approach it dispassionately or even with distaste (just like in real life you'll find people who love their job, hate their job, or fall somewhere in between.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T13:48:50-07:00","id":1405100,"title":"","content":"The main character from The Saga of Tanya the Evil would make for an excellent Devil Tiger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}